SUMMARY:Battle: Sinking of ROKS Cheonan (South Korea)
DESCRIPTION:The Sinking of ROKS Cheonan occurred on 26 March 2010\, when Ch
 eonan\, a Pohang-class corvette of South Korea\, carrying 104 personnel\, 
 sank off the country's west coast near Baengnyeong Island in the Yellow Se
 a\, killing 46 seamen. The cause of the sinking is disputed.\n\nConflict: 
 South Korea\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sinking_of_ROKS_Cheonan
 \nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
