SUMMARY:McDonald v. City of Chicago (United States)
DESCRIPTION:McDonald v. City of Chicago\, 561 U.S. 742 (2010)\, is a landma
 rk decision of the Supreme Court of the United States that found that the 
 right of an individual to "keep and bear arms"\, as protected under the Se
 cond Amendment\, is incorporated by the Fourteenth Amendment and is thereb
 y enforceable against the states.\n\nCourt ruling: United States\nSource: 
 https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McDonald_v._City_of_Chicago\nText: Wikipedia
  (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
