DESCRIPTION:Occupy Wall Street (O.W.S.) was a left-wing populist and progre
 ssive movement against economic inequality\, capitalism\, corporate greed\
 , big finance\, and the influence of money in politics. It began in Zuccot
 ti Park\, located in New York City's Financial District\, and lasted for f
 ifty-nine days—from September 17 to November 15\, 2011.\n\nProtest: Unit
 ed States\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Occupy_Wall_Street\nText:
