DTSTAMP:20261030T060403Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20120118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20120119
SUMMARY:Golan v. Holder (United States)
DESCRIPTION:Golan v. Holder\, 565 U.S. 302 (2012)\, was a US Supreme Court 
 case that dealt with copyright and the public domain. It held that the "li
 mited time" language of the United States Constitution's Copyright Clause 
 does not preclude the extension of copyright protections to works previous
 ly in the public domain.\n\nCourt ruling: United States\nSource: https://e
 n.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golan_v._Holder\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via
  PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
CATEGORIES:Court ruling
URL:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golan_v._Holder
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
