SUMMARY:2013 Bulgarian parliamentary election
DESCRIPTION:Parliamentary elections were held in Bulgaria on 12 May 2013\, 
 two months ahead of schedule. Protests had forced the resignation of the G
 ERB government in February\, leading to the election being moved up. The e
 lections resulted in a minority parliament\, with no party winning a major
 ity of seats.\n\nElection: Bulgaria\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki
 /2013_Bulgarian_parliamentary_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, v
 ia PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
