SUMMARY:Hollingsworth v. Perry (United States)
DESCRIPTION:Hollingsworth v. Perry was a series of United States federal co
 urt cases that reinstated same-sex marriage in the state of California. Th
 e case began in 2009 in the U.S. District Court for the Northern District 
 of California\, which found that banning same-sex marriage violates equal 
 protection under the law.\n\nCourt ruling: United States\nSource: https://
 en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hollingsworth_v._Perry\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.
