SUMMARY:Thirty-fourth Amendment of the Constitution of Ireland
DESCRIPTION:The Thirty-fourth Amendment of the Constitution Act 2015 amende
 d the Constitution of Ireland to permit marriage to be contracted by two p
 ersons without distinction as to their sex. Prior to the enactment\, the C
 onstitution was assumed to contain an implicit prohibition on same-sex mar
 riage in Ireland.\n\nElection: Ireland\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/w
 iki/Thirty-fourth_Amendment_of_the_Constitution_of_Ireland\nText: Wikipedi
