DESCRIPTION:On 10 October 2015 at 10:04 local time (EEST) in Ankara\, the c
 apital city of Turkey\, two bombs were detonated outside Ankara Central ra
 ilway station. With a death toll of 109 civilians\, the attack surpassed t
 he 2013 Reyhanlı bombings as the deadliest terror attack in Turkish histo
 ry. Another 500 people were injured.\n\nCrisis: Turkey\nSource: https://en
 .wikipedia.org/wiki/2015_Ankara_bombings\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\,
  via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
