DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20160102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20160103
SUMMARY:Occupation of the Malheur National Wildlife Refuge (United States)
DESCRIPTION:On January 2\, 2016\, an armed group of right-wing militants se
 ized and occupied the headquarters of the Malheur National Wildlife Refuge
  in Harney County\, Oregon\, and continued to occupy it until law enforcem
 ent made a final arrest on February 11\, 2016. Their leader was Ammon Bund
 y\, who participated in the 2014 Bundy standoff at his father's Nevada ran
 ch.\n\nProtest: United States\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Occup
 ation_of_the_Malheur_National_Wildlife_Refuge\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4
 .0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
