SUMMARY:2018 Barbadian general election (Barbados)
DESCRIPTION:General elections were held in Barbados on 24 May 2018. The res
 ult was a landslide victory for the opposition Barbados Labour Party (BLP)
 \, which won all 30 seats in the House of Assembly\, resulting in BLP lead
 er Mia Mottley becoming the country's first female prime minister.\n\nElec
 tion: Barbados\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2018_Barbadian_gener
 al_election\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
