SUMMARY:2018 Irish abortion referendum (Ireland)
DESCRIPTION:The Thirty-sixth Amendment of the Constitution of Ireland is an
  amendment to the Constitution of Ireland which permits the Oireachtas to 
 legislate for abortion. The constitution had previously prohibited abortio
 n\, unless there was a serious risk to the life of the mother.\n\nReferend
 um: Ireland\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2018_Irish_abortion_ref
 erendum\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, via PRP (jdpi.pages.dev).
