 her parts of Central Africa\, from 2018 to 2020. Between 1 August 2018 and
  25 June 2020 it resulted in 3\,470 reported cases. The Kivu outbreak also
  affected Ituri Province\, whose first case was confirmed on 13 August 201
 8.\n\nCrisis: DR Congo\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kivu_Ebola_e
